  "plain_text": "Advisory Committee on Homelessness \nOctober 27, 2026 @ 5:15 PM \nCouncil Chambers, City Hall, 73 Harlow St. \nAgenda \n1. Introductions (Name and Position Only) \n \n2. Updates \na. Warming Shelter \ni. Staff Update: On-demand warming shelter update \nii. Subcommittee Update \n \n3. Three Month Report \na. What are recommendations for highlights to include in the report? \nb. Report to include draft sections of strategic plan to ensure Committee is meeting \nCity Council expectations \n \n4. Emails and Community Communication \na. Review and discuss for 10-15 minutes each meeting. \nb. Identify information that is relevant to the strategic plan. \n \n5. Strategic Planning \na. Timeline: See proposed schedule; Plan due to Council July 14, 2027 (9 months) \nb. Format: See example \n \n6. Set discussion for next meeting (Nov. 10th) \na. See proposed schedule \nb. Updates \nNext Meeting- Nov. 10th @ 5:15PM\nProposed Strategic Plan Schedule \nDate Topic(s) \nNov. 10, 2026 Discussion on important aspects of Prevention section for strategic plan \nNov. 24, 2026 Feedback on draft strategic plan Prevention section \nDec. 8, 2026 Preliminary approval of strategic plan Prevention section \nDiscussion on important aspects of Connect section for strategic plan \nDec. 22, 2026 Feedback on draft strategic plan Connect section \nJan. 12, 2027 Preliminary approval of strategic plan Connect section \nDiscussion on important aspects of Shelter section for strategic plan \nJan. 19, 2027 Feedback on draft strategic plan Shelter section \nFeb. 9, 2027 Preliminary approval of strategic plan Shelter section \nDiscussion on important aspects of Stabilize section for strategic plan \nFeb. 23, 2027 Feedback on draft strategic plan Stabilize section \nMar. 9, 2027 Preliminary approval of strategic plan Stabilize section \nDiscussion on important aspects of House section for strategic plan \nMar. 23, 2027 Feedback on draft strategic plan House section \nApr. 13, 2027 Preliminary approval of strategic plan House section \nDiscussion on important aspects of Sustain section for strategic plan \nApr. 27, 2027 Feedback on draft strategic plan Sustain section \nMay 11, 2027 Preliminary approval of strategic plan Sustain section \nMay 25, 2027 Review and discuss complete strategic plan \nJun. 8, 2027 Public comment on strategic plan \nJun. 22, 2027 Final revisions of strategic plan \nJuly 13, 2027 Finalize strategic plan\nAdvisory Committee on Homelessness Strategic Plan Template EXAMPLE \n     Strategic Priority Area: Prevention \nGoal: Reduce the number of people entering homelessness. \nStrategies Objectives & Key Steps \nStrategy 1: Prevent evictions \n \nObjective 1: By X, develop a system for quickly \nidentifying and responding to people at risk of \neviction to prevent at least 12 evictions. \nKey Steps \n• Work with eviction court and Pine Tree legal to \nunderstand and monitor eviction trends. \n• Build relationships with landlords to refer \npeople to eviction prevention resources and \nidentify needs to support landlords. \n• Maintain Bangor Housing Navigation and \nStabilization Program. \n• Ensure timely General Assistance appointments \n \nStrategy 2: Strengthen diversion \nservices, resources, and \ncoordination. \n \nObjective 2: By X, develop and disseminate \ninformation on eviction prevention resources. \n• Identify and share information on services and \nprograms to prevent eviction. \n• Establish an eviction prevention working group \nthat meets routinely to discuss challenges and \nsolutions. \n \nPolicy Considerations • Can eviction notification be included in Bangor \nRental Registry? \nResource Considerations • Continue to include Housing Navigator and \nHomeless Response Coordinator in City budget \nto fund prevention key steps.\nAdvisory Committee on Homelessness Strategic Plan Template EXAMPLE \n     Strategic Priority Area: Connect \nGoal: Improve the efficiency and effectiveness of connecting people \nto resources